#! Signature help (s134), under the vscode profile: inside `geometry.area(3)`
#! — the cross-file callee's declared parameter, its return type and its
#! `///` doc (markdown where this client's
#! `signatureHelp.signatureInformation.documentationFormat` lists it,
#! plain text otherwise), active parameter 0; on the `if` keyword — no
#! argument list, null; inside `print("…")` — a prelude name, what the
#! checker recorded for it. One per client because the documentation
#! format is the profile's own claim.
name      annotate/signatureHelp-vscode
profile   vscode

initialize
open      resolve/two_mod/main.lu
wait      diagnostics resolve/two_mod/main.lu
req       signatureHelp resolve/two_mod/main.lu 11:21
req       signatureHelp resolve/two_mod/main.lu 11:4
open      hello.lu
wait      diagnostics hello.lu
req       signatureHelp hello.lu 10:10
shutdown
